A||||17||mrfixit58||Mobil 1 tranny fluid for Getrag -- Anyone using it?||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||12-23-2001||12:46 PM||||I'm in the process of replacing the output shaft seals in my 88 GT 5-speed and want to replace the fluid at the same time. The posi fluid that GM recommends is about $8 a quart. Mobil one is about $7 a quart. Any difference in performance. The difference of $2 is nothing but, if Mobil 1 is good and available, why not.<P>Comments?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||5
Z||000001||LZeitgeist||12-23-2001||01:13 PM||||I just switched from 5W30 motor oil in my Getrag to the GM Synchromesh fluid from the dealership ($11/quart here in NC), and it actually *does* feel smoother than I had imagined it would. I'd pop the extra couple bucks or so and go for the *real* GM stuff. Couldn't hurt... <p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadero2dmax||12-23-2001||01:16 PM||||I used Mobil 1 in my 3.94:1 Thorsen-Gleason Getrag in my racecar for years. It never let me down!!<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||12-23-2001||01:20 PM||||Using Mobil 1, just make sure you match the factory recommended weight, don't go heavier.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MoneypitGT||12-23-2001||01:30 PM||||Anybody have a part # on the Synchromesh, wondering what GMpartsdirect has it for.<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR>  <B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>Turbo Q4 GT Project||||reg||5
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||12-23-2001||01:32 PM||||I *had* the part number, but the bottles got tossed out... sorry 'bout that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||12-23-2001||02:18 PM||||I've still got my bottles of GM Synchromesh, I'll check the part number and let you know.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||12-23-2001||03:05 PM||||There's info on this in my cave.... I didn't have any data on the Mobil 1 at the time...<P>one thing to watch it the API class #. In the U.S. Gear oil usually falls into one of 2 classes.<P>GL 5 is mainly for heavy truck transmissions and Hypoid gear sets in traditional RWD axles.<P>GL 4 is used in most car transmissions.<P>Even tho the SAE weights (80w-90 etc.) of both classes are often similar, the formulation is not. GL 5 can make a car transmision difficult or imposible to shift when cold.<P>The best side by side short example is Redline's chart of tranny fluids. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||12-23-2001||03:14 PM||||Wow, Crown Pontiac in Raleigh NC ripped me and LZ off!  We paid $11 and change for each quart of Synchromesh.  According to GMPartsdirect, the GM List price is $9.42!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>Oh well.  You can get it from GMParsdirect for only $5.65 per quart, but there's a catch..... they sell it in 12 bottle cases.  You can't get it in signles.  So if you and 5 other people want to go in on a case, it's a great savings, otherwise find a dealership that won't gouge you like Crown Pontiac in Raliegh, NC.  <P>Oh, almost forgot, the part info is:<P>"GM Synchromesh Transmission Fluid"<BR>P/N: 12345349<p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000009||johnt671||12-23-2001||04:02 PM||||I went to Mobil 1 in my 84 SE 4 spd in the spring.  No problems so far.  Can't say if it helped shifting because I was having some problems and did a couple of other things at the same time.  Shifts nice now.  Your price for Mobil 1 sounds high.  Paid $4.48/qt. at Advance Auto.||||reg||1
Z||000010||lowCG||12-23-2001||06:52 PM||||I had the Mobil 1 in the gearbox for a couple weeks;didn't work that great,not much better than the 90w that someone put in there before I bought the car.<BR>I went with the GM synchromesh fluid,after trying Redline,and it shifts better than it ever had before.<BR>I'm using the stuff in full concentration,but have wondered if it was meant to work as an additive,does anyone have any info here?||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||12-24-2001||04:28 AM||||Well, I tried every fluid known to man in my Getrag.<P><BR>Then I found out our cars have some odd composite syncros, and the last fluid I tried was GM's Syncromesh.<P>P/N: 12345349<P>This is the LAST tranny fluid you will ever buy. NOTHING ELSE will work.<P>Peroid.<P>(tried Mobil-1 5w-30, Redline 5w-30, Redline MTL, and GM Syncromesh) In that order.<P>The MTL was ok, but the Syncromesh feels like a brand new gearbox.  It's awesome man.<P>Awesome.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||mrfixit58||12-24-2001||08:26 AM||||Sounds like I need to make a trip to my frendly GM parts man... after Christmas!<P>Thanks guys,<BR>Roy||||reg||14
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||12-24-2001||08:58 AM||||I just had a thought - in the spare Getrag Dad and I kept from the ;87 GT we parted out, the synchronizer from 1st to 2nd was not working properly... it would grind going into second every time.<P>Could this be a minor problem that having good (GM Synchromesh) fluid in there could take care of, or is that symptom always indicative of a part that will have to be replaced in order to improve? (I know this is vague; I'm just curious if there's an easy fix, or if new synchros will be needed before we eventually put it in his car...)<P>THanks for your thoughts...||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||12-24-2001||12:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>I had the Mobil 1 in the gearbox for a couple weeks;didn't work that great,not much better than the 90w that someone put in there before I bought the car.<BR>I went with the GM synchromesh fluid,after trying Redline,and it shifts better than it ever had before.<BR>I'm using the stuff in full concentration,but have wondered if it was meant to work as an additive,does anyone have any info here?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>GM Synchromesh is NOT an additive.  It's the correct fluid for the Munci/Getrag tranny.  Accept nothing less!  I'm sure other people have had good success with other oils.  I've used 5w30 motor oil for over a year without problem.  But until you've tried the Synchromesh, you don't know what you're missing.<P>Bottom line, IMO, it's the best for your trans.  Considering how expensive a replacement Getrag is, isn't it worth it?||||reg||14
Z||000015||theogre||12-24-2001||02:08 PM||||From Mobil 1's product data for their Gear oil...<P>Mobil 1 Synthetic Gear Lubricant is suitable for all automotive applications where lubricants meeting <u>API Service GL-5,</u> are recommended. It can also be used in rear axles where an API Service GL-4 lubricant is recommended. <u>It should not be used in any transmissions requiring an engine oil or automatic transmission fluid, or GL-4 performance level.</u><P>... That means that Mobil 1's gear oil is likely not compatible with Fiero transmissions. (I added the underlines.)||||reg||1
Z||000016||lowCG||12-24-2001||03:23 PM||||Good job,Ogre,reading between the lines there.Must be some friction reducing stuff in there or something.<BR>Thanks Formula88,had to wonder since the stuff is so thin(like brake fluid almost),nothing else will go back into my trans.||||reg||1
Z||000017||theogre||12-24-2001||04:06 PM||||If anyone is confused by gear oils, don't feel bad. Even the majority of people in parts stores can't tell you what oil to use, and that's all stores not a specific chain.<P>I spent a long time with GL5 in transmissions wondering why oil that was supposed to be for transmissions made cars almost imposible to shift right.<P>It wasn't until I finally sat down and did the cave article that I found out GL 4 and 5 are way differant animals even tho the SAE weights are often very close or the same.<P>The best way I can explain GM STF is that it's like GL4 with "limited slip" additive. That's not what it is exactly but it should give you a better idea... ||||reg||7
